      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At room temperature, the ceramic phase will provide low friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing temperature will cause controlled oxidation of the coating and formation of a stable glaze layer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC12692809::web::019::3_3_thermal_shock_performance"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-temperature glaze layer will provide solid lubrication and reduce adhesive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-temperature glaze layer will reduce abrasive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coating will maintain integrity and continuously adapt to thermal and mechanical stresses.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coated CoCrFeNi samples will have a lower coefficient of friction than uncoated CoCrFeNi throughout the full temperature range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC9960858::web::022::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coated CoCrFeNi samples will have a lower specific wear rate than uncoated CoCrFeNi throughout the full temperature range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC9960858::web::022::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-temperature tribo-oxidation can produce a protective nanocrystalline oxide glaze that provides solid lubrication and gentler wear.",
